WEBVTT

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.840
Contact Network...

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:12.420
It’s a Puzzle of Fools where the 
players must pair up to escape

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.340
or else they will get 
caught in the explosion.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.930
We are supposed to simultaneously 
extend our pipelines.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.020
If Kaito and Gammon or 
Melancholy and I connect,

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.500
only the two players in 
that team will survive.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.240
If no one escapes within the time limit,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:29.000
the puzzle will explode 
and all four of us will...

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.010
There is no doubt about 
it. Kaito is in Room B.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.070
But those moves...

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.010
What is Kaito trying to accomplish?

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:42.090
It’s no use! I can’t figure it out!

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.020
It’s beyond me now that 
I’ve given up puzzles!

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.790
What should I do?

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:57.250
But if I don’t figure 
it out, Melancholy will...

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.800
I still haven’t made 
amends with her...

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:08.000
Melancholy, there is no 
way I will let you die!

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.010
Mama, give me courage!

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:49.020
Farewell Forever

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.320
Freecell...

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.320
Kaito... Gammon...

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:01.660
All three of you, catch on!

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.410
I need everyone’s help or

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.210
we’re gonna get blown to smithereens.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.410
I get it! I see what 
Kaito is getting at.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.280
I already know where Kaito is.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.420
It’d be easy for us to 
hook up and walk outta here.

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.180
But Kaito...

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.930
It’s useless. I just don’t get it!

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:29.140
Freecell, I’m a goner, aren’t I?

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.140
Please catch on, Melancholy!

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.230
Is that... a signal?

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.890
So that’s the deal? 
There was a loophole?

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.080
Is Kaito Daimon trying to 
save all four of us...?

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:50.540
This is what you want me to do, right?

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.150
She did it!

00:04:01.150 --> 00:04:02.050
Melancholy!

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:03.550
Let’s get outta here!

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:07.810
Crap! Did we tick off the puzzle?

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.140
Hurry!

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:16.710
Kaito! Gammon!

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:19.440
Freecell!

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:29.070
That was a close call!

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.710
We made it out by the skin of our teeth.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:32.330
Freecell!

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.080
I’m glad you’re all right.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.060
I owe it to Kaito.

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.710
Thank you, Kaito.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.320
You truly are amazing.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:44.150
Meh. That wasn’t 
half bad for DaiMORON.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.990
You should be singing me 
praises about right now!

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:47.280
Ahem!

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:50.700
Aren’t you forgetting about someone?

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:57.960
Melancholy!

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:59.820
What are you doing way up there?

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:02.160
A perfectly valid question!

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:05.200
I got caught in the blast 
and before I knew it...

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.470
Y-ya don’t say...

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.750
Hey, isn’t this great? 
Everyone’s okay!

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:12.200
There is nothing “great” about this.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:16.100
An excellent opportunity to avenge 
myself came knocking on my door,

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.960
but all three of you came out unscathed.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.410
Cut the tough act!

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:23.890
Enigma nearly snuffed you out 
along with the rest of us.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:26.320
I had anticipated as much.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.910
That puzzle was rigged 
so I could slip out.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:30.970
Say what?!

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:33.650
But I’ve had my fill!

00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:36.120
I’ll let my game of 
vengeance end here.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.510
This time I mean it when 
I kiss those detestable

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:39.980
puzzles goodbye forever.

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:41.480
“Detestable puzzles”?

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:44.200
Jin Makata’s Puzzles of Fools...

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:46.860
Do you think anyone in the 
world likes those things?

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:48.630
Melancholy...

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:52.740
You’re such a dimwit!

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:57.730
It’s obvious that an Orpheus 
Ring forced him to make them!

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.900
Even if the Armlet consumed him,

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.520
Jin would never make 
that kind of puzzle!

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:04.250
Shouldn’t you know better 
than anyone how untrue that is?

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.380
Rook and Freecell!

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:10.190
Think of what your two friends 
did because of their Armlets...

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.560
That’s right. The 
Orpheus Ring is to blame.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:18.320
But in my case...

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.520
I didn’t change at all 
when I wore the Armlet!

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:26.380
Maybe Jin Makata is evil after all!

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:27.760
You imp!

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.580
Are you trying to be 
nice or a total brat?!

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.200
I appreciate your coming 
all of the way from Japan.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:38.540
Since you’re here anyway, why 
don’t you drop by my place?

00:06:38.730 --> 00:06:39.980
What?!

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.540
Where did that come from?

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:45.310
If you like, we could 
have dinner together.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.240
Sound good, Freecell?

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:55.620
Why on earth did they agree?!

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.710
I can’t believe they’re 
going to Melancholy’s house!

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:00.620
What are Kaito and the guys thinking?!

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.840
They said they wanted 
to travel in lux-lux.

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.500
So there you have it!

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:07.300
What precisely is that 
supposed to mean?!

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:11.300
<i>Melancholy hates Kaito, 
Freecell and puzzles.</i>

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.270
It’s dangerous! Too dangerous!

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:16.450
She must have set some sort of trap!

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.460
It is an honor to have 
you visit our abode.

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:26.980
It-it’s huge! This is your house?

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:29.470
Are you actually a real noblewoman?

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:32.720
Pretty much. I do hail from nobility.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.600
I had no idea... I never knew.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.420
Did you expect me to 
tell you my life story?

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:42.040
Nana, we have guests!

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.860
I don’t care to go any 
farther than this, you know?

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.170
Same, but...

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:50.430
Freecell said that he wants 
to use this as an opportunity

00:07:50.430 --> 00:07:51.860
to make up with Melancholy.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:55.370
But I personally think that 
she is partially at fault.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:59.450
Regardless, it doesn’t change 
the fact that I hurt her.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:01.600
She is the only one

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:04.690
who hasn’t been freed 
from her nightmarish past.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:07.380
We’re back to our normal 
lives, but not her!

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.540
Freecell can’t turn a 
blind eye on the poor girl!

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:11.260
Ya know?

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.640
I swear, everyone is so 
stinkin’ nice it hurts!

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:16.760
Let’s go!

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.260
Yum! This is good!

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:35.640
Is it an urban legend that 
England’s food is super nasty?

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:42.350
Uh, er, well, you see, I meant...

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:43.310
Problem?

00:08:43.310 --> 00:08:44.040
I’m sorry.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:48.170
What a silly young lady!

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.170
I hear that a lot!

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:56.200
It looks like you didn’t 
poison the grub.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:00.080
Don’t expect to find your typical 
nobility tropes around here.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:03.120
Okay, okay! ’Scuse me for 
bein’ an ignorant commoner!

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.790
She seems to be in a pretty good mood.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:09.010
Yeah, but I don’t know 
how she truly feels.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.820
She won’t let us 
peer into her heart...

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:16.070
What’s up?! Somethin’ going down?

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.160
It’s just your average blackout.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.390
We get them around these 
parts from time to time.

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:23.430
Gramps, fetch some candles.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.830
Most certainly.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:37.020
Huh? Then you live here by yourself?

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:39.950
I have Gramps and Nana here with me.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.410
My parents passed away 
when I was little.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:43.680
Do you have any relatives?

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.600
Just one uncle.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:50.110
But he’s out receiving medical 
treatment thanks to a certain someone.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:54.690
Aren’t you lonely?

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.610
You’re all alone in 
this massive house...

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:58.820
Wouldn’t you like some friends?

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:02.370
Not really! I think friends 
are a pain in the neck.

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:04.210
I see...

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:10.670
Melancholy, I...

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.530
How could I make it up to you...?

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.010
I think it’s about time 
I retired for the evening.

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:28.890
Everyone, feel free to take your time.

00:10:29.380 --> 00:10:31.270
That said, please see to them for me.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.290
Most certainly.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:38.030
Well then, good night.

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:47.350
The Little Lady is most resilient.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.710
Her cheerful smile never falters,

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.470
despite living in this 
lonesome, remote area.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:07.350
I’m telling you, Melancho isn’t 
making any friggin’ sense!

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.330
It wouldn’t surprise me if

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:11.510
you said that this blackout 
is part of some trap.

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.730
But I don’t think it is.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.730
I wouldn’t be so sure.

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:22.780
I thought... she looked 
awfully little...

00:11:37.740 --> 00:11:41.330
I would be lonely if I were her...

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.440
Please use the room down there.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:50.690
Thank you.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:53.550
I hope you sleep well.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:55.270
Good night.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.530
Let’s call it a night.

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:07.240
I’m sure that eventually

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.040
Melancholy will come to 
realize how you feel.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.150
I hope you’re right...

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:23.610
Aren’t these...?

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:26.540
Are all of these puzzles?

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:34.690
You led them to the eastern bedroom?

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:37.690
Yes. Is there a problem?

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.200
Awesome!

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:54.460
All of these are good puzzles!

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.500
I feel the same way.

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:03.970
Strangely, they make me want 
to solve each and every one...

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:07.950
I was scared.

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:10.460
I have been distancing 
myself from puzzles.

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.470
The memories were too 
painful to do otherwise.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:17.620
But sure enough, they are fun!

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:18.530
They’re great fun!

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:21.230
I love puzzles.

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:23.020
That right?

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:24.630
Freecell...

00:13:27.050 --> 00:13:29.470
But isn’t it strange?

00:13:30.110 --> 00:13:32.320
Of all places, I’ve rekindled my love

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:34.500
for puzzles in Melancholy’s home.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:36.920
Yeah, that is kinda funny.

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:38.560
I don’t get it!

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:42.500
Malancho told us that she hates puzzles.

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:44.740
If she hates them so 
much, why does she have

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:46.320
so many in her home?

00:13:46.320 --> 00:13:47.860
That’s simple enough!

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:53.410
To become a Master Brain, I made 
them as part of my training.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.640
Fighting the urge to barf,

00:13:56.400 --> 00:13:58.040
I made those vile puzzles!

00:13:58.420 --> 00:13:59.830
I don’t believe you.

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:01.650
Excuse me?

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:04.830
All of the puzzles you made 
are kind, warm puzzles.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:09.660
You don’t hate a single 
one of these puzzles!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.910
Don’t tell me, Melancholy, 
that you’re...

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:33.640
Stop it! Melancholy, stop it!

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:38.390
Please stop, Melancholy!

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:40.310
Let go!

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.310
I had a shining future,

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:46.580
but you and puzzles stole that from me!

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:49.240
That’s not something I can forgive!

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:04.110
I was being optimistic...

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:08.540
Melancholy hates me... and puzzles...

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:10.470
from the bottom of her heart.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.220
You really think so?

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:17.750
I think she forgave you a long time ago.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:19.440
After all...

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:23.080
That’s right. The 
Orpheus Ring is to blame.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:27.400
She fully understands what happened.

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:29.900
Nonoha...

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:33.820
But it doesn’t change 
the fact that she became a

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.910
Master Brain for a chance 
to avenge herself.

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:39.310
There’s no telling what’s 
runnin’ through her head.

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:50.920
Sorry I gathered you up so early.

00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:54.920
Nah, we were up all night 
thinking about them ourselves.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.180
Those poor, burnt puzzles...

00:15:57.830 --> 00:15:59.450
At the very least, let’s bury them.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.730
Sound good?

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.210
Melancholy...

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:09.190
What’s she up to?

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:13.320
I’m sorry... I treated you horribly.

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:17.570
But, this is me...

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:20.210
This is me.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:24.390
She was lonesome, sure enough...

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:28.130
That’s why she made 
all of those puzzles.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:37.470
E-everyone, may I help you?

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:45.480
Melancholy, would you be 
willing to become our friend?

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:49.110
Wouldn’t you like that, Freecell?

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:54.330
Melancholy, I may have hurt you and

00:16:54.330 --> 00:16:56.350
torn you away from your uncle,

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:59.950
but even so, we can 
still become friends!

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:08.110
What is with that overbearing attitude?

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.460
Whether we’re friends or 
not is for me to decide.

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:13.800
A long time ago,

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.690
I was like you and only 
had puzzles for friends.

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:19.850
You’re lonely by 
yourself, aren’t you?

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.350
I’ve finally figured out the reason 
why you became a Master Brain.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:27.330
It wasn’t for somethin’ 
like revenge.

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:29.610
It was ’cause you’d get to see 
Freecell along with the rest of us!

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:32.610
Isn’t that right, Melancholy?

00:17:33.170 --> 00:17:35.360
You should be more honest with yourself!

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.870
Kaito, you’re pushing it.

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:40.960
You’re such a pain!

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:48.630
I can’t stand people who try to 
trample their way into others’ hearts.

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:52.420
My answer is “No.”

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:56.010
You will never see me again.

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:57.760
Melancholy!

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:04.670
That’s the end of that.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.520
She smashed her last chance 
with her own two hands.

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:15.400
Kaito, help me!

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:16.900
With what?

00:18:17.510 --> 00:18:19.150
I’m not about to give up!

00:18:19.150 --> 00:18:21.160
Not as long as I can 
do something for her!

00:18:21.850 --> 00:18:22.830
Freecell...

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.740
This house is so big and empty...

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:15.840
Freecell, you’ve got a 
good look in your eyes.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:19.280
Yeah. It’s like aren’t the 
same person you were yesterday!

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:20.930
You think so?

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.050
Don’t worry!

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:23.660
I’m sure Melancho’ll be just fine.

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:27.780
Someday, she’ll meet 
someone who will change her.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:31.160
Just like how someone 
changed Cubik, Ana and I.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:32.230
Huh?

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:35.770
Er, uh, well... Oh, I know!

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:37.670
Freecell, you should 
go out with Melancho!

00:20:37.980 --> 00:20:38.810
What?!

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:43.300
Yes?

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:21.560
I solved it!

00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:26.770
“Dear Obstinate Puzzle-Friend, 
We will meet again!”

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:32.970
I won’t let you off the hook!

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:44.960
I’m sorry.

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:47.820
I shouldn’t have gone after 
your prey without asking first.

00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:51.210
It was our chance to eliminate

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:53.950
several of the Phi-Brain 
children in one shot.

00:21:54.690 --> 00:21:57.100
Yes, I will avoid doing 
that in the future.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:58.530
I’m going now. Sweet dreams.

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:08.510
Something’s off... Something 
isn’t right here!

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:19.080
The Phi-Brain children 
are most impressive.

00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:23.480
But that is precisely what 
makes them worth hunting.

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:27.360
Isn’t that right, Lovushka?

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:04.320
Upperclassman, your car sure is cool!

00:24:04.730 --> 00:24:07.230
You can tell? It’s a good car!

00:24:07.230 --> 00:24:09.490
It gives a sense of freedom all its own.

00:24:09.650 --> 00:24:11.970
But running off of gasoline 
is a thing of the past.

00:24:12.240 --> 00:24:13.670
If I were you, this is 
how I’d fix it up.

00:24:15.410 --> 00:24:18.750
Now it’s the only car in the 
world that runs off of apple juice.

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:20.920
Let’s drive to the airport!

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:23.650
Next time, “Let’s 
Go to That Place.”

00:24:22.330 --> 00:24:27.980
Let’s Go to That Place

00:24:24.040 --> 00:24:27.210
Driving gives a sense of 
excitement all its own!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:30.990
Fin Art: Akeru Otsuki
